+
+---
+
+## Findings
+
+### 1. Discord link in the HUD breaks Community Standards. Blocker
+
+**Where:** `Hud.luau:135-145`, the `Community` label: "Join our Discord for free codes!
+discord.gg/blockbuilders".
+
+**What goes wrong:** Experience UI "may not link to, share, or display URLs of any external websites
+or services", and other efforts to send users off Roblox are prohibited [standard]. That puts the
+whole experience at risk of moderation, and the audience is mostly children. The label is also 20 px
+tall and uses `TextScaled`, so on a phone it's unreadable, and it sits at the bottom middle between
+the player's thumbs (P9).
+
+**Fix:** Delete the label. The only allowed route is Social Links on the experience or group page,
+which needs an owner age-checked 16+ [standard]. If codes stay a feature, announce them in-game,
+for example through a codes field in Settings. Don't gate on
+`PolicyService.AllowedExternalLinkReferences`: it always returns an empty array [standard].
+
+### 2. Menu buttons are blank orange squares, and their names show only on hover. Blocker
+
+**Where:** `Hud.luau:27-31` (`Icon = "rbxassetid://0"` for all three) and `Hud.luau:62-69` and
+`117-133` (the name appears only in a hover tooltip).
+
+**What goes wrong:** The three buttons look the same, and their names appear only on
+`MouseEnter`. Touch and gamepad have no hover, so phone and Xbox players have to guess what each
+button does. That's most of the audience. Children recover from confusion by leaving [study], and
+players should be challenged by the game, "not in trying to figure out what icons mean"
+[practitioner]. Even with icons, an icon alone is weaker than an icon with a word (P2, P5).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Give every button an icon and a short word that are always visible: "Bag", "Settings",
+  "Rewards". Put the label under or beside the icon, using a fixed `TextSize` (see #10).
+- Until the art is uploaded, ship text-only buttons. Don't ship blank squares.
+- Make the tooltip a PC-only extra, or drop it. Hover should only preview something a tap or
+  gamepad focus also shows [inference].
+
+### 3. No gamepad path to the HUD or the popup. Blocker
+
+**Where:** `Hud.luau:70` and `DailyReward.luau:113, 159` use `MouseButton1Click`. Nothing sets a
+selection, a `SelectionGroup`, or a Back binding.
+
+**What goes wrong:** `MouseButton1Click` is mouse-only, and gamepad A doesn't fire it. `Activated`
+covers mouse, touch, and gamepad A [standard]. No screen sets a default selection either. On Xbox
+the popup opens on join with nothing focused, so the player can't claim or close it without
+finding Roblox's UI-navigation toggle. The menu rail can't be reached at all. XAG requires UI that
+is "fully navigable by keyboard and controller digital input alone" [standard] (P5).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Switch every button to `Activated`.
+- **Popup:** when it opens, call `GuiService:Select` on the panel with Claim as the first pick
+  (`SelectionOrder`). Wrap the panel in a `SelectionGroup` with `SelectionBehavior = Stop` so focus
+  stays inside. Map B to Close. Check that the B binding wins over Roblox's own B in the Controller
+  Emulator; the docs don't say [unverified]. When the popup closes, return focus to the element
+  that opened it (for example the Rewards button).
+- **HUD:** bind one gamepad button (for example ButtonY or DPadUp) through `ContextActionService`
+  to open a menu hub, or to move focus onto the rail with a `SelectionGroup` set to `Escape`. Show
+  the glyph next to the rail on gamepad, taken from `UserInputService:GetImageForKeyCode`. Don't
+  hardcode Xbox art.
+- Give every selectable a visible focus state (`SelectionImageObject` or a stroke).
+
+### 4. Menu rail sits in the jump-button corner. High
+
+**Where:** `Hud.luau:102-106`, with `AnchorPoint (1, 1)` at `(1, -12, 1, -12)`, which is the
+bottom-right corner.
+
+**What goes wrong:** On touch, the bottom-right corner belongs to the jump button and the player's
+right thumb [standard]. Players will hit Rewards or Settings when they mean to jump, and jump when
+they mean to open a menu. A bottom-right rail also lands near Roblox's `SendNotification` toasts
+[standard] (P3, P7).
+
+**Fix:**
+- **Phone:** a vertical rail on the right edge, centered around 40-50% of the screen height, clear
+  of the jump button. Roblox's sample puts a custom action button 20 px left of jump, so check the
+  real jump position from `TouchGui` in the emulator.
+- **Tablet:** the same rail moved lower, but still above the jump button. A button 40% down from
+  the top is hard to reach on a tablet [standard].
+- **PC and Xbox:** a right-edge or bottom-middle rail is fine there.
+- Choose the layout from `PreferredInput` (see #17).
+
+### 5. Daily reward popup blocks play as soon as the player joins. High
+
+**Where:** `Main.client.luau:22`, `rewardOpen = source(true)`, plus the full-screen dim frame with
+`Active = true` at `DailyReward.luau:71-77`.
+
+**What goes wrong:** The first thing a new player sees is a modal, not the game. Players try 24 or
+more experiences a month and decide "within minutes" [standard]. A popup before any play costs some
+of those players, and new players have no streak to care about anyway (P1).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Don't auto-open. When a reward is waiting, put a badge on the Rewards button (a dot or "1", see
+  #13) and optionally show a short toast at the top: "Daily reward ready!".
+- If design wants the popup to open by itself, open it at a natural pause: after the first block is
+  placed, or on the second session onward. Never open it in a new player's first seconds.
+- Test this as an Experiment that compares the badge with auto-open on D1 retention and claim rate
+  (see the playtest and funnel questions).
+
+### 6. 59-second countdown and "lose your streak" threat aimed at kids. High
+
+**Where:** `Main.client.luau:16, 24, 74-79` (a 59-second countdown) and the copy at
+`DailyReward.luau:142`: "Claim in 0:59 or lose your 6-day streak! Come back every day so you don't
+lose your progress."
+
+**What goes wrong:** A ticking clock plus loss wording is the pressure pattern our guidelines rule
+out for a young audience. ICO Standard 13 is the working bar, and it forbids nudges that work
+against a child's interests [standard; inference]. The timer also misleads: it reaches 0:00 and
+nothing happens, and Claim still works. The paragraph is two sentences and over 100 characters,
+which children skip [study] (P9, P2).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Remove the countdown and the loss wording.
+- Replace the copy with one line: "Day 7: 50 coins!" After the claim, show "Next reward tomorrow".
+  A time-until-next is fine if it's informative and not a threat, for example "Next reward in 14h".
+- As a design change, consider streaks that pause instead of reset when a day is missed
+  [inference]. That keeps the goal-gradient pull of the 7-day row [study] without the threat.
+
+### 7. Coin counter sits under Roblox's top bar. High
+
+**Where:** `Main.client.luau:53` sets `IgnoreGuiInset = true` (which switches the ScreenGui to
+`DeviceSafeInsets`), and `Hud.luau:90` puts Coins at `(8, 8)`, the top-left corner.
+
+**What goes wrong:** The top-left is where Roblox draws its menu and chat buttons. With the inset
+ignored, "Coins: 250" renders under them, so the one number the player tracks is partly covered
+(P4).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Remove `IgnoreGuiInset` and set `ScreenInsets = Enum.ScreenInsets.CoreUISafeInsets` on the HUD
+  ScreenGui. Give the dim backdrop its own ScreenGui with `ScreenInsets = None` so it still covers
+  the whole screen.
+- Move coins to the top middle or top right, below `GuiService.TopbarInset`. Read the inset and its
+  changed signal live. Never hardcode 36 or 58 px: the height "may vary based on device and screen
+  size" [standard].
+
+### 8. Touch targets are well under the minimum size. High
+
+**Where:** `Hud.luau:18` (36 px on touch, 32 px otherwise, with 6 px gaps), `DailyReward.luau:105`
+(Close is 24 x 24), and `DailyReward.luau:151` (Claim is 120 x 36).
+
+**What goes wrong:** Children aged 7-11 miss touch targets 46% of the time, against 32% for adults
+[study]. Our floor is 10 mm for any tap target and 15-20 mm for primary actions [study;
+practitioner], which is 44 or more in our 1080-tall design units with a root `UIScale`
+[practitioner]. A 24 px Close in the corner of a panel is the hardest target on the screen. Small
+targets at screen edges should be avoided for children [study] (P3).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Rail buttons: about 64 x 64 on touch (icon plus label), with 8-12 px gaps.
+- Claim, the primary action: about 220 x 72.
+- Close: at least 56 x 56 hit area. The visible "X" can stay smaller inside a larger transparent
+  button.
+- Size everything in 1080-tall design units under one root `UIScale`. The Vide skill's
+  `references/screens.md` owns that module.
+
+### 9. Popup text and buttons fail contrast. High
+
+**Where:** `DailyReward.luau:16-21`. Ratios computed with the WCAG formula:
+
+| Element | Colors | Ratio | Needed |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Streak text and Close "X" | grey 150 on panel 240 | about 2.6:1 | 4.5:1 |
+| "DAILY REWARD!" title | orange (255,170,0) on panel 240 | about 1.7:1 | 3:1 (large text) |
+| "CLAIM" and today's day number | white on green (80,200,90) | about 2.2:1 | 3:1 (large text) |
+| Future day numbers | white on grey 200 | about 1.7:1 | 3:1 |
+| Claimed day numbers | white on grey 130 | about 3.9:1 | passes for large text only |
+
+**What goes wrong:** Most of the popup fails XAG 102 [standard]. The title and future days are close
+to invisible for low-vision players and on dim phone screens outdoors (P6).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Body text: dark grey (around 60,60,60) on the light panel, about 7:1.
+- Title: a darker orange (around 200,100,0), or keep the bright orange and give it a dark
+  `UIStroke`.
+- Claim button: a darker green (around 30,130,50) with white text, or keep the green and use dark
+  text.
+- Day numbers: dark text on light tiles.
+- Re-check every pair with a contrast checker after the change.
+
+### 10. `TextScaled` everywhere: ignores the player's text size, and the streak paragraph shrinks to tiny text. High
+
+**Where:** every TextLabel and TextButton in both files.
+
+**What goes wrong:** `TextScaled` opts a label out of `GuiService.PreferredTextSize`, the Roblox
+setting players use to make text bigger [standard]. It also sizes each label to its own box, so
+labels end up at different sizes [practitioner]. The streak sentence (`DailyReward.luau:132-145`) is
+crammed into a 64 px box with `TextWrapped`, so it shrinks to whatever fits, which is tiny on a
+phone. The coin label shrinks as the number grows (P6).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Define one `TextSize` per role, for example title 40, body 24, label 20 and caption 18 in
+  1080-tall units. Body text should be at least 26 at 1080p on console [standard].
+- Use `AutomaticSize` on containers so text at Largest grows them instead of clipping.
+- Cut the paragraph to one line (see #6).
+- Verify at `PreferredTextSize = Largest` in the emulator.
+
+### 11. Day tiles show state by color only and don't show the reward. Medium
+
+**Where:** `DailyReward.luau:37-63`. Claimed, today, and future are grey, green, and light grey,
+with nothing else to tell them apart.
+
+**What goes wrong:** Color never carries meaning alone [standard] (XAG 103). Claimed grey (130) and
+future grey (200) are also easy to confuse. Each tile shows only its day number, not what the
+player gets, so the 7-day row doesn't show the goal it's meant to pull toward. Seeing progress
+toward a reward is what makes people speed up [study] (P6, P2).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Claimed tiles get a checkmark.
+- Today's tile is larger, gets a thick outline, and is labeled "Today".
+- Future tiles stay plain or get a small lock.
+- Every tile shows a reward icon and amount ("50"). Make day 7 visibly bigger if its reward is.
+
+### 12. Claim never switches to a claimed state, so it can be claimed again. Medium
+
+**Where:** `Main.client.luau:35-48`. The Rewards button reopens the popup, and Claim always pays out
+and increments the streak. After day 7, the row has no day 8 and every tile goes grey.
+
+**What goes wrong:** The button has no claimed or disabled state, so the player gets no clear
+"done", and pressing Rewards again pays out again. After day 7 the row stops making sense. A
+progression button should never change what it does or seem to work when it shouldn't [standard,
+secondary] (P7, P8).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Give the popup two states:
+  - Reward ready: Claim is enabled.
+  - Claimed: the button is disabled and reads "Claimed!", with a checkmark on today's tile and
+    "Next reward tomorrow" below.
+- Define what happens after day 7: either the row restarts at day 1 with "Week 2", or day 7 repeats.
+- Separately, outside this UI review: claiming has to be server-authoritative. Right now coins and
+  the streak live only on the client.
+
+### 13. Rewards button pulses forever. Medium
+
+**Where:** `Hud.luau:48-53`, where a `Heartbeat` connection scales the button every frame, whether
+or not a reward is waiting.
+
+**What goes wrong:** Motion pulls the eye [study], so a button that never stops moving competes with
+building. It keeps pulsing after the reward is claimed, which teaches players to ignore it. It
+ignores `ReducedMotionEnabled` [standard]. It also redraws the whole HUD ScreenGui every frame
+[practitioner, measured in our performance guidance] (P8).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Replace the pulse with a static badge (a red dot or "1") shown only while a reward is ready.
+- When the reward becomes available, play one pop (about 200 ms, ease out). With
+  `ReducedMotionEnabled`, skip the pop and just show the badge.
+- Remove the `Heartbeat` connection.
+
+### 14. Reward toast lasts 1.5 s, sits mid-screen, and is the only feedback. Medium
+
+**Where:** `Main.client.luau:15` (`TOAST_SECONDS = 1.5`) and `Hud.luau:147-163` (orange text with no
+backplate at 40% from the top, in the center).
+
+**What goes wrong:**
+- 1.5 s is too short for young readers. Our toast floor is about 6 s [practitioner].
+- Orange text over the 3D world has no guaranteed contrast.
+- The center of the screen is where the player is looking to build.
+- Claiming is the game's reward moment, and right now it is just the popup vanishing plus a brief
+  line of text. Rewards should use two or three channels [inference from study], and medium juice
+  beats none [study] (P8, P6).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Toast: at the top or upper middle, below the coins. Use a dark backplate with white text, at
+  least 6 s on screen, and one toast at a time. Merge repeats, so two "+50" toasts become one
+  "+100".
+- Claim moment:
+  - Today's tile pops and gets its checkmark (about 200 ms).
+  - Coin icons fly to the coin counter, and the counter ticks up with a short scale bump.
+  - A coin sound plays.
+- The whole claim moment lasts under 500 ms. With `ReducedMotionEnabled`: no flying coins, just a
+  fade and the sound.
+
+### 15. Inventory and Settings buttons do nothing when pressed. Medium
+
+**Where:** `Main.client.luau:45-46`, which only calls `print`.
+
+**What goes wrong:** A press that gives no response reads as broken, and children recover from
+errors by leaving [study] (P8).
+
+**Fix:** Hide the buttons until their screens exist. If they have to ship, have a press show a toast
+such as "Coming soon!" within 100 ms.
+
+### 16. Coin counter has no backplate and a fixed-width box. Medium
+
+**Where:** `Hud.luau:88-100`, white "Coins: 250" with a transparent background in a 140 px box.
+
+**What goes wrong:** White text over the 3D world fails contrast over sky, snow, or a light
+baseplate. It has to pass against the least-contrasting part of the background [standard]. The
+word "Coins:" takes room the number needs, and large numbers will shrink the text (P6).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Show a coin icon plus the number, on a semi-opaque dark pill. Alternatively, white text with a
+  2 px dark `UIStroke`.
+- Use `AutomaticSize = X` on the pill.
+- Abbreviate large numbers to about three significant digits ("12.5K"), using one suffix table for
+  the whole game [inference].
+
+### 17. Layout is chosen with `TouchEnabled`, and sizes don't adapt to TVs. Medium
+
+**Where:** `Hud.luau:17-18`, plus fixed pixel offsets throughout, with no root `UIScale`.
+
+**What goes wrong:** `TouchEnabled` is true on touch laptops and handhelds, so it doesn't mean
+"phone" [standard]. It's also read once at load. `PreferredInput` changes at runtime, for example
+when a PC player picks up a controller. On Xbox, at 8-10 feet, 32 px buttons and `TextScaled` text
+are too small, and key UI has to stay inside the TV-safe area [standard] (P4).
+
+**Fix:**
+- Choose the touch, gamepad, or mouse layout from `UserInputService.PreferredInput`, and
+  re-evaluate when it changes.
+- Detect TVs with `GuiService.ViewportDisplaySize == Large` (not the deprecated
+  `IsTenFootInterface`). On TVs, scale up and keep a margin of about 5% from the edges. The 5% is
+  industry habit; Roblox gives no figure [inference].
+- Author in 1080-tall units under one root `UIScale`, per the Vide skill's `references/screens.md`.
+
+### 18. Small items. Low
+
+- **Fonts:** Gotham was removed in May 2024 and replaced with Montserrat [standard]. Switch to
+  Builder Sans, the platform font, so the text looks the way you intended.
+- **Tooltip position** (`Hud.luau:123`): it's always placed by the bottom row, whichever button is
+  hovered. If the PC tooltip stays, anchor it to the hovered button.
+- **Dim backdrop** (`DailyReward.luau:75`): multiply its transparency by
+  `GuiService.PreferredTransparency` and update on change [standard].
+- **Tap outside:** the popup isn't destructive, so a tap on the dim area could close it, the same as
+  Close [inference]. Test whether kids expect this.
+- **Popup entrance:** none today. Add a 200-300 ms ease-out scale or fade in and a shorter exit,
+  with a fade-only version for reduced motion [practitioner].
+
+---
+
+## What works (keep it)
+
+- The 7-day row is a strong goal shape. Visible progress toward a reward makes people speed up
+  [study]. Keep it and make it richer (#11).
+- Claiming takes one tap, the HUD is small (coins plus three buttons), and only one toast shows at
+  a time. Keep all three while fixing the rest.
+
+## Questions for a playtest or funnel
+
+1. **Auto-open vs badge:** run an Experiment (roughly 1,000 daily users or more are needed to read
+   it [standard]) comparing the popup opening on join with a badge on the Rewards button. Measure
+   D1 and D7 retention and daily claim rate.
+2. **Can players find menus?** In a playtest with about 5 new players aged 7-12 on phones, ask them
+   to "open your rewards" and "change a setting". Note mis-taps on the rail and accidental jumps.
+3. **Xbox:** in the Controller Emulator and on hardware, can a player claim, close the popup, and
+   open each menu with the D-pad, A, and B alone, without a hint?
+4. **Funnel events:** `reward_popup_shown`, `reward_claimed`, `reward_closed_unclaimed`,
+   `menu_opened{name}`. These show whether the popup is claimed or dismissed, and which rail
+   buttons get used at all. Cut any button players don't use every session.
+5. **Streak design:** compare pause-on-miss with reset-on-miss on 7-day return rate, once the threat
+   copy is gone.
